# Business Requirements Document (BRD)

## 1. Project Information

**Project Name:** E-commerce Sales Performance & Customer Behaviour Analysis

**Company:** xyz Online Retail Ltd. (Fictional)

**Project Role:** Junior Business Analyst

**Project Status:** In Progress

## 2. Business Background

xyz Online Retail Ltd. is an e-commerce company experiencing inconsistent sales performance.

The company wants to better understand its sales trends, product performance and customer purchasing behaviour.

Currently, the business lacks sufficient insights to make informed decisions about sales improvement and customer retention.

## 3. Business Problem

The company faces the following challenges:

- Inconsistent monthly sales performance.
- Limited understanding of customer purchasing behaviour.
- Lack of visibility into top,low performing products.
- Difficulty identifying valuable customer segments.
- Limited data driven insights for business decisions.

## 4. Business Objectives

The main objectives are:

1. Analyse overall sales performance.
2. Identify the highest and lowest performing products.
3. Understand monthly revenue trends.
4. Analyse customer purchasing behaviour.
5. Identify opportunities to improve customer retention.
6. Provide recommendations to improve business performance.

## 5. Project Scope

### In Scope

- Sales data analysis.
- Product performance analysis.
- Customer behaviour analysis.
- Revenue trend analysis.
- Country wise sales analysis.
- Data visualisation and reporting.
- Business recommendations.

### Out of Scope

- Developing a new e-commerce website.
- Implementing a payment system.
- Managing inventory operations.
- Launching marketing campaigns.
- Changing the company's existing IT infrastructure.

## 6. Business Requirements

| ID | Business Requirement | Priority |
|---|---|---|
| BR01 | The business needs to monitor overall sales performance. | High |
| BR02 | The business needs to identify top-performing products. | High |
| BR03 | The business needs to understand monthly revenue trends. | High |
| BR04 | The business needs to analyse customer purchasing behaviour. | High |
| BR05 | The business needs to identify sales performance by country. | Medium |
| BR06 | The business needs a dashboard to visualise key business metrics. | High |

## 7. Success Criteria

The project will be considered successful when:

- Sales performance has been analysed.
- Top- and low-performing products have been identified.
- Customer purchasing patterns have been evaluated.
- Revenue trends have been visualised.
- A Power BI dashboard has been developed.
- Actionable business recommendations have been documented.

## 8. Assumptions

- Historical sales transaction data will be available.
- The dataset contains relevant product and customer information.
- Sales data can be analysed using Excel, SQL and Power BI.
- The analysis will be based on the available historical data.

## 9. Deliverables

- Business Requirements Document.
- Stakeholder Analysis.
- Data Cleaning and Analysis.
- SQL Queries.
- Power BI Dashboard.
- Business Recommendations.

## 10. Conclusion

This project aims to provide ABC Online Retail Ltd. with meaningful insights into sales performance and customer purchasing behaviour.

The findings will help management make informed business decisions and identify opportunities for improvement.
